-# systemd at all: with cgroup v2 delegation (user@.service, Delegate=yes)
-# this process's parent slice (app.slice) is writable by us and already
-# enables the memory controller for children. So: create a sibling child
-# cgroup under that parent — the same shape systemd-run would create —
-# write memory.max/memory.swap.max, migrate THIS wrapper into it (children
-# inherit), run, migrate back, rmdir. Requires only a cgroupfs path grant
-# (nono profile 1.13.0). If any step is not permitted we fall through to
-# systemd-run; the wrapper is never silently uncapped by this path.
-# Sibling-not-child: cgroup v2's no-internal-processes rule forbids enabling
-# controllers under a cgroup that has processes (our own scope does).
